# Godot 4
.godot/
/android/

# `export_presets.cfg` is TRACKED, which is the opposite of the usual advice.
#
# It is normally ignored because it is where a keystore path and a keystore
# password end up, and a repo that carries those is a repo that leaks them. The
# file in this project carries neither: the three release-signing fields are
# empty on purpose and the header says so. What it does carry is the exclude
# filters, the architectures, the billing permission and the package name —
# decisions worth keeping in history, and worth a diff when one of them moves.
#
# THE RULE THAT MAKES THAT SAFE: never put a credential in it. If you fill in
# `keystore/release` or `keystore/release_password` on your machine, that line
# does not get committed. `tests/test_export.gd` fails if either is non-empty.

